description:
Second instance of the manual_let_else idiom in crate-jmap-sharing-server, sibling to the closed bd:JMAP-3t94.36.

Location: crate-jmap-sharing-server/src/lib.rs:474-481 in MockBackend::destroy_object (inside the lib.rs test module's MockBackend impl).

Current shape:

```rust
let acct = match guard.get_mut(account_id.as_ref()) {
    Some(a) => a,
    None => {
        return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(
            SetErrorType::NotFound,
        )))
    }
};
```

clippy::manual_let_else (implied by -W clippy::pedantic) fires here.

Idiomatic rewrites:

(a) let-else:
```rust
let Some(acct) = guard.get_mut(account_id.as_ref()) else {
    return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(SetErrorType::NotFound)));
};
```

(b) ok_or_else + ?:
```rust
let acct = guard.get_mut(account_id.as_ref())
    .ok_or_else(|| BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(SetErrorType::NotFound)))?;
```

Form (a) preferred here — there is no .cloned() involved, no atomic-on-failure concern, and the immediate-borrow shape (acct is held for the next few lines) is cleaner as let-else than as ?-with-binding.

Why this was not folded into .36: the .36 bead's stated scope was memory.rs:664-676. AGENTS.md Scope and Style requires that every change trace directly to the task. Filing as a sibling bead keeps the .36 close cleanly within its stated scope.

Workspace propagation: the same shape may exist in sibling crates' test-module MockBackend impls. A workspace-sweep bead can pick this up alongside the memory.rs propagation that .36's bead body mentions.
